{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-118759",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HQR+m∠PQR & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HQR+{105}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HQR & ={75}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△QHR$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QRH+m∠HQR+m∠RHQ & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH+{75}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH+{165}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH & ={15}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
